<%# Public product surface: explain what Kurukoo helps people get done. Internal implementation terms stay out of the user's path. %>
<%- include('_partials/head', { pageStyles: ['/css/kurukoo-public-pages.css?v=8'] }) %>
<%- include('_partials/nav') %>
<main class="public-composition public-composition--features container" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <section class="public-feature-hero">
    <div class="public-feature-hero__copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">What Kurukoo can do</span>
      <h1 id="features-title">Tell Kurukoo what you need. Let it help.</h1>
      <p>Kurukoo helps you get things done. Tell it what you need, want, notice, or are worried about. It works out what it can do, takes appropriate action, gets help when needed, keeps you informed, and remembers what matters.</p>
      <div class="public-feature-hero__actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/chat">Ask Kurukoo</a>
        <a class="public-return-link" href="/how-it-works">See how it helps</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="public-feature-lifecycle" aria-labelledby="feature-lifecycle-title">
      <span class="eyebrow">From need to outcome</span>
      <h2 id="feature-lifecycle-title">You start with the outcome. Kurukoo works out the route.</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Tell it</strong><p>Use your own words. You do not need to choose a category first.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Let it work</strong><p>Kurukoo uses the information, tools, services, devices or people available to help.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Know what happened</strong><p>Kurukoo gives you the result, what it still needs, or the next useful step.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="public-feature-section" aria-labelledby="features-help-title">
    <div class="public-feature-section__heading"><span class="eyebrow">Help directly</span><h2 id="features-help-title">Sometimes Kurukoo can solve the problem with you.</h2><p>When the available device, service or connected resource gives Kurukoo what it needs, it can check, explain, organise, diagnose, monitor or safely act instead of sending you somewhere else first.</p></div>
    <div class="public-feature-grid">
      <article class="public-feature-card public-feature-card--featured"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#chat"></use></svg><h3>Ask Kurukoo</h3><p>Describe the problem or goal naturally. Kurukoo keeps the useful context together and works out what to do next.</p><a href="/chat">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      <article class="public-feature-card"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#settings"></use></svg><h3>Check your technology</h3><p>Ask Kurukoo to check supported phones, tablets, computers, TVs, networks and connected devices. It uses only information and controls actually available to it.</p><a href="/chat?prompt=Check%20my%20device">Ask for a device check <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      <article class="public-feature-card"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#discover"></use></svg><h3>Find useful things</h3><p>Find services, people, places, products, events and opportunities that can help with what you are trying to do.</p><a href="/discover">Explore Discover <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      <article class="public-feature-card"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#tasks"></use></svg><h3>Keep things moving</h3><p>Turn conversations into reminders, tasks, follow-ups and ongoing work without starting again.</p><a href="/tasks">Explore tasks <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="public-feature-section public-feature-section--split" aria-labelledby="features-coordinate-title">
    <div class="public-feature-section__heading"><span class="eyebrow">Get help when needed</span><h2 id="features-coordinate-title">If Kurukoo cannot do it alone, it can help find who can.</h2><p>A request can move from direct assistance to another person, business, service, agent or physical participant without making you repeat the whole story.</p></div>
    <div class="public-feature-grid public-feature-grid--compact">
      <article class="public-feature-card"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#package"></use></svg><h3>Requests</h3><p>Turn a need into an explicit request and keep its progress, decisions and outcome together.</p><a href="/requests">See your Requests <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      <article class="public-feature-card"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#channels"></use></svg><h3>People and services</h3><p>When a human or external service is needed, Kurukoo can coordinate the appropriate participant when a supported path exists.</p><a href="/network">Explore the network <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      <article class="public-feature-card"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#memory"></use></svg><h3>Remember what matters</h3><p>Keep useful preferences and context connected to your relationship with Kurukoo when you choose to.</p><a href="/memory">Manage Memory <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      <article class="public-feature-card"><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#channels"></use></svg><h3>Stay connected</h3><p>Use Chat and supported channels to receive updates and continue the same work when you return.</p><a href="/channels">See channels <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="public-feature-boundary" aria-labelledby="feature-boundary-title">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Trustworthy help</span><h2 id="feature-boundary-title">Kurukoo tells you what it knows and what it could not do.</h2><p>Important actions can require your permission. External providers, device access, payment, delivery and other consequential outcomes are only presented as completed when the relevant state and evidence exist.</p></div>
    <div class="public-feature-boundary__links"><a href="/safety"><strong>Safety</strong><span>Keep important help and permissions under your control</span></a><a href="/memory"><strong>Memory</strong><span>Choose what useful context Kurukoo keeps</span></a><a href="/how-it-works"><strong>How it works</strong><span>See what happens from your point of view</span></a></div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('_partials/footer') %>
